{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1770,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is a misconception about chameleons\nthat they change their color in order to blend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5890,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in with their environment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8200,
    "dDurationMs": 2349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is actually not the case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10549,
    "dDurationMs": 5740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When a chameleon is calm it is green and so\nit naturally blends in with its leafy surroundings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16289,
    "dDurationMs": 4991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But male chameleons change color when they\nbecome excited in the presence of a female"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21280,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a rival male, as shown here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23580,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I will put the first frame in the bottom right\nfor comparison."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27200,
    "dDurationMs": 5329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you can see, as he becomes more excited,\nhis color changes to be more yellow orange"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32529,
    "dDurationMs": 1441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and red."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33970,
    "dDurationMs": 4030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead of blending in this chameleon will\nnow stand out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38000,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how do chameleons actually change their\ncolor?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41590,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For years we thought that there was a simple\nwell-established mechanism for this color"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45680,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46680,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In their skin, chameleons have different cells\ncontaining colored pigments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50850,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some are yellow others are red and some contain\nthe dark melanin pigment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56010,
    "dDurationMs": 4730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Many animals including chameleons are known\nto turn a darker shade by causing the melanin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60740,
    "dDurationMs": 3589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to spread out along the fingery extensions\nof the cell."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64329,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They turn lighter again by condensing the\npigment back into one spot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68509,
    "dDurationMs": 5161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was assumed that chameleons must turn yellow,\norange and red in the same way, by causing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73670,
    "dDurationMs": 3009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those pigments to spread out in those cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76679,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But new research from collaborating groups\nof physicist and biologists at the University"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80789,
    "dDurationMs": 3481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Geneva shows that this is incorrect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84270,
    "dDurationMs": 4279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the first clue should come from the fact\nthat there is actually no green pigment in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88549,
    "dDurationMs": 1081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the a chameleon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89630,
    "dDurationMs": 6619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The green color actually created by two distinct\nmechanisms, pigment color and structural color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96249,
    "dDurationMs": 6070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Beneath the yellow pigment cells, there are\ncells containing tiny 130 nm crystals regularly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102319,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "arranged in a lattice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104099,
    "dDurationMs": 4361,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now light diffracts off these crystals and\ndue to the spacing between them, blue light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108460,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "constructively interferes and is therefore\nstrongly reflected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112250,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whereas the other colors are not reflected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115030,
    "dDurationMs": 4819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is very similar to how a morpho butterfly\nwing creates an iridescent blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119849,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is no blue pigment just the periodic\nnanoscale structure that acts as a strong"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124569,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reflector for only one color."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127299,
    "dDurationMs": 4541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a chameleon looks green due to the combination\nof the yellow light from the pigment plus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131840,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the blue light reflected off the crystal structure\nbeneath it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135120,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how do chameleons change this green into\nyellow orange and red?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139670,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well previously it was assumed that the color\nchange was achieved by dispersing pigments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144060,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the colored cells."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145810,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now scientists have found it's actually\nthe crystals underneath which are changing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151030,
    "dDurationMs": 6110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By increasing the spacing between the crystals\nthe chameleons can change which color is selectively"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157140,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reflected."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158140,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bigger gaps between the crystals are better\nat reflecting longer wavelengths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162220,
    "dDurationMs": 7290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as the spacing increases, the color changes\nfrom blue to green to yellow, and then orange"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169510,
    "dDurationMs": 1670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and red."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171180,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists compared skin samples from calm\ngreen chameleons and excited yellow chameleons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175730,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and found that indeed, in the excited chameleon\nthe crystal spacing was much further apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182170,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here you can see a single cell enlarged and\nthe color it reflects changing from blue to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187630,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "green to yellow, orange and red."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191000,
    "dDurationMs": 6150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plus, a computer simulation of the light reflected\noff crystals while their spacing is decreasing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197150,
    "dDurationMs": 3130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also provides excellent agreement with these\nobservations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200280,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Furthermore, applying physical pressure to\nthe skin causes the crystals to compress and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205540,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they reflect more blue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207620,
    "dDurationMs": 5199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When that pressure is removed, the crystals\nexpand again reflecting more green light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212819,
    "dDurationMs": 4301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The structure of a chameleon’s skin gets\neven more fascinating, as there is another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217120,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "layer of cells underneath which also contain\ncrystals."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220820,
    "dDurationMs": 5170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But these crystals are larger more spaced\nout and more disorganized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225990,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means they reflect longer wavelengths\nin the infrared part of the spectrum and they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230320,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reflect a broader range of these wavelengths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232830,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s thought that the function of this layer\ncould be to reflect light from the sun since"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237130,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these chameleons live in bright full-sun habitats."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240880,
    "dDurationMs": 5530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So male chameleons don't change their color\nby spreading out red and yellow pigments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246410,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead they do something much more remarkable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249030,
    "dDurationMs": 6289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They actively tune the spacing between nanoscale\ncrystals in order to create structural colors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255319,
    "dDurationMs": 3381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that span the whole length of the visible\nspectrum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258700,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now what I find amazing is that in this day\nand age we thought we had the answer to how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262930,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chameleons change color, but it actually took\nthe combined expertise of physicists and biologists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267900,
    "dDurationMs": 7880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "working together to figure out what's really\ngoing on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275780,
    "dDurationMs": 5270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This episode of Veritasium was supported by\nLinda.com a leading online learning platform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281050,
    "dDurationMs": 5850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with over 3000 video courses taught by experts\nin areas ranging from video production to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286900,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "web development and computer programming."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289500,
    "dDurationMs": 4069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chances are if you can think of a topic, they\nhave a course that teaches it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293569,
    "dDurationMs": 4861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now as part of this sponsorship they are offering\nVeritasium viewers a 10 day free trial of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298430,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any and all courses on the site."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300710,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just go to Lynda.com/Veritasium or click the\nlink in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304840,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know one of the courses I’m really interested\nin is Adobe After Effects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307960,
    "dDurationMs": 2989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s a really good animating software."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310949,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right now I still do all of my animations\nincluding the ones in this video in Final"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314849,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cut Pro which is really tedious and time consuming."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317469,
    "dDurationMs": 3531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if you’re interested in learning how\nto program maybe you should try out their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321000,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Java courses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322340,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those are really good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323800,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or if like me you’ve always wanted to do\nmore with Photoshop, you should try out one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327300,
    "dDurationMs": 2639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their Photoshop or photography courses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329939,
    "dDurationMs": 4062,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you want to learn something new today,\nyou should go to Lynda.com/Veritasium for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334001,
    "dDurationMs": 1329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "10 days free trial."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335330,
    "dDurationMs": 1639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There’s really nothing to lose me."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336969,
    "dDurationMs": 3711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I really want to thank Lynda.com for supporting\nme, and I want to thank you for watching."
    } ]
  } ]
}
